# Mariner: land on an airless body (the Moon, Mercury) from
# orbit, on the lander's own engine.
#
# In orbit with the upper stage spent (or nearly): plan a
# "Come down" burn on the map (M, Maneuver, Suggested: its
# periapsis at the ground), then send this.

# Leave the upper stage, keep the shield (stage 3), arm the
# parachute (4: nothing to catch here), drop the shield and
# light the lander (5).
stage
wait 3 s
stage
wait 1 s
stage
log Lander free

sas maneuver
burn

# Fall until the braking burn must start, then brake hard.
sas retrograde
wait until brake < 2 s
log Braking
throttle full

# Slow: come down briskly (hovering costs fuel), then
# gently (legs down), then touch down softly.
wait until speed < 40 m/s
descend 25 m/s
wait until altitude < 1 km
legs down
descend 8 m/s
wait until altitude < 100 m
descend 2 m/s
wait until landed
throttle off
sas hold
log Landed
panels out
science
transmit
